{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(_:)-1udyo","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(_:)-2xtcf","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(_:)-7fh5d","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(_:)-8whsh","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(_:)-98jdd","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(cPointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(constPointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(gconstpointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(gpointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(mutating:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/init(opaquePointer:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/ptr"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/PointerWrapper-Implementations","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef\/StaticMutexProtocol-Implementations"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StaticMutexRef","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"StaticMutexRef","externalID":"s:4GLib14StaticMutexRefV","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StaticMutexRef"}]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"StaticMutexRef","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prior to GLib 2.32, GStaticMutex had the significant advantage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that it doesn’t need to be created at run-time, but can be defined"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"at compile-time. Since 2.32, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" can be statically allocated"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as well, and GStaticMutex has been deprecated.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here is a version of our ","type":"text"},{"code":"give_me_next_number()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" example using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"a GStaticMutex:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["  int","  give_me_next_number (void)","  {","    static int current_number = 0;","    int ret_val;","    static GStaticMutex mutex = G_STATIC_MUTEX_INIT;","","    g_static_mutex_lock (&mutex);","    ret_val = current_number = calc_next_number (current_number);","    g_static_mutex_unlock (&mutex);","","    return ret_val;","  }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sometimes you would like to dynamically create a mutex. If you don’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"want to require prior calling to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_thread_init()"},{"type":"text","text":", because your code"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"should also be usable in non-threaded programs, you are not able to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_mutex_new()"},{"type":"text","text":" and thus "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex"},{"type":"text","text":", as that requires a prior call to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_thread_init()"},{"type":"text","text":". In these cases you can also use a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It must be initialized with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_mutex_init()"},{"text":" before using it","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and freed with with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_mutex_free()"},{"type":"text","text":" when not needed anymore to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"free up any allocated resources."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Even though "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","type":"reference"},{"text":" is not opaque, it should only be used with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the following functions, as it is defined differently on different"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platforms.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All of the g_static_mutex_* functions apart from"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_mutex_get_mutex()"},{"type":"text","text":" can also be used even if "},{"code":"g_thread_init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"has not yet been called. Then they do nothing, apart from"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_static_mutex_trylock()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" which does nothing but returning ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All of the g_static_mutex_* functions are actually macros. Apart from","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"taking their addresses, you can however use them as if they were","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef"},{"type":"text","text":" type acts as a lightweight Swift reference to an underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStaticMutex"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It exposes methods that can operate on this data type through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef"},{"text":" only as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unowned"},{"text":" reference to an existing ","type":"text"},{"code":"GStaticMutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (instead of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") if you want to use Automatic Reference Counting for memory management of the underlying ","type":"text"},{"code":"GStaticMutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/staticmutexref"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex"},{"type":"text","text":" works like a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/do